Wait, let me reconsider this. The modified files are only TypeScript React components (`Login.tsx` and `Dashboard.tsx`), which are source code files. There are no build artifacts, dependency directories, or temporary files in the change list that would require ignoring.

Actually, since only source code files (`.tsx`) are being modified and no build artifacts or dependencies are present in the changes, the optimized approach would be to keep it minimal and only include common TypeScript/React project ignores that are likely needed for this type of project.

```gitignore
# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build outputs
dist/
build/
*.js.map
